      "side": 1,
      "message": "My mental model is that minSdkVersion is one concept and thus the field and the method shouldn\u0027t do different things. \n\nThe reason why I thought this is slightly better is that it puts the decision about -target closer to the module that is being compiled and makes it easier to understand what the Min_sdk_version / Sdk_version fields mean.\n\nMy medium-term plan is to simplify the way the \"sdk\"/\"version\" mutators work so that the dependency graph is slightly simpler (I sent you the document alreadY) and then I hope that CRT modules won\u0027t need to be special-cased; that will make this a bigger win. WDYT?",
      "parentUuid": "ed813a58_3c727623",
      "revId": "1521cb4b9822df081e3c89e1bbacdd165c5f7143",
