      "writtenOn": "2021-06-17T19:42:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Am I spreading the \"CRT-ness\" wider? This change only replaces the mysterious \"split by API levels\" concept with the less-mysterious \"is CRT\" one, which I thought was an improvement.\n\nI don\u0027t understand the \"breaking anything else that uses ctx.minSdkVersion()\" argument: it doesn\u0027t, because this change only affects the CRT libraries? (or maybe I misunderstand what you mean by \"it\" in this sentence?)\n\nWhat this particular line does is that it embodies the \"For a given Sdk_version / Min_sdk_version pair, every library needs -target to be the Min_sdk_Version *except* CRT which has to be built with Sdk_version\". And it makes some sense to have that logic where the command line is put together instead of somewhere far away?",
      "parentUuid": "d3c68acf_67a8f296",
      "revId": "1521cb4b9822df081e3c89e1bbacdd165c5f7143",
